    "modelReasoning": "Swaps pass because addition mod 10 is commutative: a digit sum ignores order. Give each position a distinct nonzero weight and work modulo 11, a prime: a single wrong digit changes the sum by weight x difference, nonzero mod 11 because every nonzero element is invertible, and an adjacent swap changes it by (w1 - w2)(a - b), also nonzero. Luhn misses 09/90; doubling every digit mod 10 keeps the symmetry and maps 0 and 5 together."
